<!--
    kuna infrastructure test: DWARF variant-part import (`option dwarfvariants`).

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 program-prep, external-refinement (the DWARF importer).
    P0 assertion:      option dwarfvariants on|off  (default on).

    A Rust tagged enum carries NO `DW_TAG_member` of its own: its whole layout
    lives under a `DW_TAG_variant_part`, whose `DW_AT_discr` names the
    discriminant member and whose `DW_TAG_variant` children carry a
    `DW_AT_discr_value` plus the variant's named payload struct. The sibling
    `dwarfstructs` import (DIV-86) walks `DW_TAG_member` children and therefore
    recovered a Rust enum's `DW_AT_byte_size` and ZERO fields.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Both passes clear it
    and load the same real x86-64 ELF fixture
    (`decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/dwarfvariants_x86_64`,
    `rustc 1.90.0 -C debuginfo=2 -C opt-level=1`, source vendored beside it),
    because a `bytechunk` carries no DWARF at all and this decision is made
    inside `load file`. The gate is read at load time, so the `option` line comes
    BEFORE the `load file` in each pass.

    Pass 1 (`option dwarfvariants off`) reproduces the bug:
      * `ret_result` is `fn(u32) -> Result<u32,u32>`, 8 bytes. A field-less
        aggregate has no width the ABI classifier can place, so it is treated as
        a hidden-return-buffer call: a phantom `rethidden` first parameter
        appears, the real parameter shifts one slot right, and the body then
        reads `x` out of the phantom.
      * `ret_three` is a 16-byte three-variant enum. That IS a real sret, so the
        parameters do not move, and what is lost is the layout: the discriminant
        and each variant's payload are written as raw byte offsets
        (`field_0x4`, `field_0x8`).

    Pass 2 (the shipped default, `option dwarfvariants on`) reproduces the fix:
      the discriminant is a named `tag` field, each variant's payload is a named
      union facet carrying the SOURCE variant name (`A`, `B`), and `ret_result`
      recovers the signature its source declared.

    The NEGATIVE: `ret_pair` returns a plain C-shaped `struct Pair { u32 lo, hi; }`
    from the same image. No C aggregate carries a variant part, so it must render
    IDENTICALLY in both passes; `ret_plain` is the same for a FIELDLESS enum,
    which rustc emits as a `DW_TAG_enumeration_type` that this pass never sees.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option dwarfvariants off</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/dwarfvariants_x86_64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function ret_result</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function ret_three</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function ret_pair</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function ret_plain</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option dwarfvariants on</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/dwarfvariants_x86_64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function ret_result</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function ret_three</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function ret_pair</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function ret_plain</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="DWARFVARIANTS #1: off, a field-less enum return is misclassified as a hidden-return buffer" min="1" max="1">ret_result\(core::result::Result&lt;u32, u32&gt; \*rethidden,uint4 x\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="DWARFVARIANTS #2: on, the recovered layout gives the classifier a width and the source signature comes back" min="1" max="1">core::result::Result&lt;u32, u32&gt; ret_result\(uint4 x\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="DWARFVARIANTS #3: off, the discriminant is a raw byte offset" min="1" max="1">\*\(unsigned int \*\)rethidden = 0;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="DWARFVARIANTS #4: on, the discriminant is the named tag field DW_AT_discr pointed at" min="1" max="1">rethidden-&gt;tag = 0;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="DWARFVARIANTS #5: off, a variant payload is a raw byte offset" min="1" max="1">\*\(uint4 \*\)&amp;rethidden-&gt;field_0x4 = x;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="DWARFVARIANTS #6: on, variant A's payload carries the SOURCE variant name, not a synthesized one" min="1" max="1">\(rethidden-&gt;payload\)\.A\.__0 = x;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="DWARFVARIANTS #7: on, and so does variant B, so three variants are not two" min="1" max="1">\(rethidden-&gt;payload\)\.B\.__0 = \(uint8\)x;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="DWARFVARIANTS #8: a plain C-shaped struct in the same image renders identically in BOTH passes" min="2" max="2">fx::Pair ret_pair\(uint4 x\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="DWARFVARIANTS #9: and so does a fieldless enum, which rustc emits as an enumeration type this pass never sees" min="2" max="2">Plain ret_plain\(uint4 x\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="DWARFVARIANTS #10: no variant name is ever synthesized" min="0" max="0">Variant0</stringmatch>
